rns a loss per batch element instead and ignores size_average. Default: True reduction (str, optional)  Specifies the reduction to apply to the output: 'none' | 'mean' | 'sum'. 'none': no reduction will be applied, 'mean': the sum of the output will be divided by the number of elements in the output, 'sum': the output will be summed. Note: size_average and reduce are in the process of being deprecated, and in the meantime, specifying either of those two args will override reduction. Default: 'mean' Shape: Input: (N,D)(N, D)(N,D) or (D)(D)(D) where DDD is the vector dimension. Output: A Tensor of shape (N)(N)(N) if reduction is 'none' and input shape is (N,D)(N, D)(N,D); a scalar otherwise. Examples: >>> triplet_loss = nn.TripletMarginLoss(margin=1.0, p=2, eps=1e-7) >>> anchor = torch.randn(100, 128, requires_grad=True) >>> positive = torch.randn(100, 128, requires_grad=True) >>> negative = torch.randn(100, 128, requires_grad=True) >>> output = triplet_loss(anchor, positive, negative) >>> output.backward() forward(anchor, positive, negative)[source]# Runs the forward pass. Return type Tensor
